<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Backstab</h1>
<p>Skill
Class: Assassin (guild level 0), Thief (guild level 0, up to 50%)
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>backstab &lt;character&gt;
</pre>
<p>You slip up behind someone who isn't expecting it and drive a blade into 
their back. A backstab that lands strikes as if the victim wore no armour 
at all, so it can do terrible damage, and it starts the fight on your 
terms.
</p><p>You must wield a dagger, a short sword or a stiletto; other weapons won't 
do. You can't backstab someone who is already fighting. A sleeping victim 
can't resist at all; an awake one resists with their dexterity and their 
own skill against yours. Once stabbed, a victim stays wary: for about a 
quarter of an hour, every backstab tried on them is much harder than the 
last. A failed backstab misses, and the fight is on.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
